-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",61,{
[1921]="7000B8A1\n1\tTalk to Calenglad and confront Mordrambor about Narchuil\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Calenglad has decided that you and he may learn of Narchuil's power or history by confronting Mordrambor together, and such knowledge may aid you to recover it before Amarthiel does.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Mordrambor has escaped from the keep on Tinnudir. Many Rangers were slain during his passage, and Calenglad now seeks to hold together the Dúnedain in the face of these losses.\n",
[1922]="7000B8A2\n1\tCollect Annúminas city-stones (total: 8)\tStones from the buildings of Annúminas can be found all throughout the great city and would be ideal for constructing cairns in memory of the fallen Rangers. Calenglad has asked you to collect stones from throughout the streets of the City of the Kings with which to make cairns for Tadan, Colhamnir, and Carchammadel.\n2\tBring Annúminas city-stones to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have collected stones from Annúminas to use in the building of cairns for the Rangers slain during the escape of Mordrambor and should return now to Calenglad.\n",
[1923]="70037826\n1\tTalk to Háma and he will bring you before the King\tHáma has grudgingly decided to allow you in to see the King, and will bring you inside the Golden Hall if you speak to him once more.\n2\tTalk to Gandalf within Meduseld\tYou have reunited with Gandalf within the Golden Hall of Meduseld, and should now speak to the Wizard.\n",
[1924]="7000B8A3\n1\tTalk to Calenglad and travel with him to Barad Rath\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have been invited to join the Dúnedain in remembering their kin slain by Mordrambor during his escape.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. The remembrance of the fallen Dúnedain was interrupted by the appearance of a raven sent by Torogethir: Amarthiel's troops have begun their search for Narchuil.\n",
[1925]="7003782A\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in Meduseld\030Talk to Gimli in Meduseld\030Talk to Legolas in Meduseld\tAragorn, Legolas, and Gimli wait to speak with you within the Golden Hall of Meduseld.\n2\tTalk to Théoden in Meduseld\tThéoden is more willing to listen to you, now that Gandalf has spoken words of truth to the King of Rohan.\n3\tTalk to Háma outside Meduseld\tThéoden has asked you to bring his commands to Háma, outside the Golden Hall.\n",
[1926]="70037830\n1\tFind the entrance to Gríma Wormtongue's chambers in Edoras\tGríma Wormtongue's former chambers can be found north-east of the bottom of the Meduseld steps, in Edoras.\n2\tGríma's chambers can be found north-east of the bottom of the Meduseld steps, in Edoras. How many secrets remain to be discovered within Wormtongue's chambers?\t\n3\tHow many secrets remain to be discovered within Wormtongue's chambers?\t\n4\tHow many secrets remain to be discovered within Wormtongue's chambers?\t\n5\tUnlock the chest in Gríma's chambers\tHow many secrets remain to be discovered within Wormtongue's chambers?\n6\tPresent to Háma the stolen items you recovered in Gríma's chambers\tHáma should be told what you discovered in Wormtongue's chambers.\n7\tShow the stolen items you recovered to Gríma in Meduseld\tYou found a number of stolen items in Gríma Wormtongue's chambers, and should confront him with them.\n8\tShow the stolen items to Théoden, in Meduseld\tYou found a number of stolen items in Gríma Wormtongue's chambers, and should now present them to the King.\n",
[1927]="7000B8A4\n1\tLook to the east atop Amon Raith\030Find the summit of Amon Raith\tAmon Raith is a tall hill in the North Downs, south-east of the Fields of Fornost and north-east of Trestlebridge. Calenglad has asked you to travel to the summit of Amon Raith and to look eastward from the heights.\n2\tLook to the east atop Weathertop\030Find the summit of Weathertop\tAmon Sûl, the great hill of Weathertop, is located in the Lone-lands. Calenglad has asked you to travel to the summit of Weathertop and to look eastward from the heights.\n3\tTalk to Alphlanc\tLooking eastward from the summit of Weathertop, you saw a company of Angmarim crossing the Last Bridge into the Trollshaws. You have followed a company of Angmarim eastward, and they have reached the Last Bridge before you. You should travel to the Last Bridge and speak with the scout posted there for news of the Angmarim.\n4\tTalk to Candelleth\tEchad Candelleth is in Tâl Bruinen, south of the Ford of Bruinen. Alphlanc told you to locate the path south along the banks of the Bruinen, and to follow the path until you come across one of Candelleth's scouts, who can further guide you to the camp. Alphlanc has told you that the Angmarim company passed into Tâl Bruinen and wants you to travel to her sister Candelleth's camp in order to warn her of the danger posed by the presence of the Angmarim.\n",
[1928]="7000B8A5\n1\tDefeat Angmarim Scout (total: 6)\030Defeat Angmarim Searcher (total: 3)\tSmall ruins can be found scattered throughout the wooded hills and valleys of Tâl Bruinen. Candelleth told you that the Angmarim seem to have a great interest in the various small ruins found throughout Tâl Bruinen. While you confront several of these searching groups, she will consider places where Narchuil may have been hidden.\n2\tTalk to Candelleth\tCandelleth is at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen. You have defeated several of the searching Angmarim and should now return to Candelleth to see if she has any information on where Narchuil may have remained hidden.\n",
[1929]="700378B8\n1\tReturn Éowyn's favour to her in Meduseld\tÉowyn is within the Golden Hall of Meduseld. Théoden has removed an embroidered handkerchief from the collection of stolen goods you recovered from Wormtongue's chambers, and wants you to return it to its original owner: his niece Éowyn.\n2\tFind the entrance to Éomer's chambers\tÉowyn has asked you to return her favour to her brother Éomer, currently imprisoned at his chambers, north of Meduseld, in Edoras.\n3\tBring Éowyn's favour to her brother Éomer\tÉowyn has asked you to return her favour to her brother Éomer, currently imprisoned at his chambers, north of Meduseld, in Edoras.\n4\tStudy the map in Éomer's chambers\tEven imprisoned, Éomer has continued to plan for the defence of Rohan. He has asked you to study the map in his chambers so you may better understand the geography of the Kingdom.\n5\tTalk to Éomer in his chambers\tWhen you have fully studied the map in Éomer's chambers, you should return to him to learn what he thinks of the strategic situation in Rohan.\n6\tTalk to Éowyn in Meduseld\tÉowyn is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld. Éomer has asked you to return to his sister, and to thank her for her sympathy and her worry.\n7\tTalk to Gandalf in Meduseld\tGandalf is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld, and he will likely have some advice for you.\n",
[1930]="7000B8A6\n1\tInvestigate Eryn Singor with Lavanthir\030Investigate Delossad with Muildir\tMuildir is outside the narrow pass through the rocks to Delossad, south-east of Echad Candelleth. Lavanthir is outside the entrance to Eryn Singor, home of the Wood-trolls in north-west Tâl Bruinen. Candelleth has told you of two locations in Tâl Bruinen that possess an unsavoury air: a set of ruins called by the Elves Delossad, and the home of the wood-trolls at Eryn Singor. Two of her scouts, Muildir and Lavanthir, are investigating these locations, and she has asked you to consult them for guidance.\n2\tTalk to Candelleth\tCandelleth is at Echad Candelleth in Tâl Bruinen. You have investigated both Eryn Singor and Delossad, but have found no sign of Narchuil. Candelleth is waiting to hear of your progress.\n",
[1931]="700378B9\n1\tTalk to Théoden and see if he is willing to step outside his hall\tThéoden is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld. Gandalf has asked the King to step outside the Golden Hall and look upon the city. You should speak now to Théoden and see if he is willing to do as the Wizard entreats.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn in Meduseld\030Talk to Éomer in Meduseld\030Talk to Gandalf in Meduseld\tAragorn, Éomer, and Gandalf are within the Golden Hall of Meduseld. Théoden King has determined his next course of action, and those who follow him have their orders.\n3\tTalk to Théoden in Meduseld\tThéoden is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld, waiting to speak with you about his next course of action: war!\n4\tTalk to Éowyn in Edoras, outside Meduseld\tÉowyn is outside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras.\n",
[1932]="7000B8A7\n1\tFind the entrance to Bar-e-Therchir\tThe entrance to Bar-e-Therchir is somewhere within Eryn Singor, home of the Wood-trolls in the north-west region of Tâl Bruinen. Lavanthir believes that the unpleasant air that hangs over Eryn Singor emanates from the cave of Bar-e-Therchir and wants you to find the entrance, defeating Wood-trolls along the way, and then return to him.\n2\tFind south-west room in Bar-e-Therchir\030Find northern room in Bar-e-Therchir\030Defeat Dâg Taushakhu (total: 2)\tThe Dâg Taushakhu live within the deepest chambers of Bar-e-Therchir, located within Eryn Singor, home of the Wood-trolls in the north-west corner of Tâl Bruinen. Lavanthir has asked you to search the deepest chambers of Bar-e-Therchir to see if Narchuil lies hidden there and to defeat the Dâg Taushakhu.\n3\tTalk to Lavanthir\tLavanthir is outside Eryn Singor, home of the Wood-trolls in Tâl Bruinen. You have defeated the Dâg Taushakhu deep within Bar-e-Therchir, but found no sign of Narchuil.\n",
[1933]="7000B8A8\n1\tFind the locked door deep within the ruins of Delossad\tThe door that leads deeper into Delossad is in the rear of the ruins south-east of Echad Candelleth. The Angmarim have been searching Tâl Brunien for some clue to Narchuil's location. Muildir has asked you to check that the door that leads deeper into the ruins of Delossad is secure.\n2\tTalk to Muildir\tMuildir is keeping watch outside the ruins of Delossad, south-east of Echad Candelleth. You have determined that the door leading further into the ruins of Delossad remains secure. The Angmarim have not yet managed to open it. You should return now to Muildir with this news.\n",
[1934]="700378BA\n1\tRead the proclamation aloud at the market north of Meduseld\tÉowyn has given you a proclamation to read at the market north of Meduseld, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.\n2\tConvince Anwynd to obey the word of Théoden\030Convince Baduhild to obey the word of Théoden\tSeveral of the people at the market north of Meduseld need to be convinced of the wisdom of Éowyn's plan.\n3\tRead the proclamation aloud at the stairs north-west of Meduseld\tÉowyn has given you a proclamation to read at the top of the stairs, north-west of Meduseld, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.\n4\tTalk to Ethryth atop the stairs north-west of Meduseld\tEthryth is atop the steps north-west of Meduseld, and has sought to catch your eye.\n5\tPick up Ethryth's belongings\tEthryth's belongings are at the top of the stairs north-west of Meduseld. The waggon to Dunharrow is near the outside walls to the north of Ethryth.\n6\tRead the proclamation aloud at the entrance courtyard in the north-west of the city\tÉowyn has given you a proclamation to read by the entrance courtyard in the north-west, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.\n7\tTalk to Derláf at the entrance courtyard in the north-west of Edoras\tA small child, Derláf, has sought to get your attention.\n8\tTalk to a growling dissenter\tGrowling dissenters insulted the King at the courtyard near the north-west entrance to Edoras.\n9\tRead the proclamation aloud at the courtyard with two stairs, south of the north-west entrance to the city\tÉowyn has given you a proclamation to read at the two stairs south of the north-west entrance, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.\n10\tConvince Colinan to obey the word of Théoden\030Convince Herith to obey the word of Théoden\tSeveral of the people at the courtyard with two stairs need to be convinced of the wisdom of Éowyn's plan.\n11\tReturn the proclamation to Éowyn outside Meduseld\tÉowyn is outside Meduseld, in Edoras. You have helped prepare the people of Edoras prepare to leave their city, and should return to Éowyn with a report of your success.\n",
[1935]="7000B8A9\n1\tTalk to Idhreneth\tIdhreneth is near the Crumbled Cellar, not far to the north-east of Echad Candelleth. Candelleth has asked you to speak with one of her scouts who defeated a number of Angmarim by the Crumbled Cellar.\n2\tUse Pile of Debris\tThe Crumbled Cellar is north-east of Echad Candelleth. Idhreneth defeated a small company of Angmarim she found searching the debris of the Crumbled Cellar and has asked you to search the ruins for some sign of what they were looking for.\n3\tBring rotted diary to Idhreneth\tIdhreneth is across the water from the Crumbled Cellar, north-east of Echad Candelleth. You have found a rotted diary among the debris of the Crumbled Cellar, but it still appears readable. You should read it and show it to Idhreneth.\n4\tBring rotted diary to Candelleth\tCandelleth is at the Elf-camp of Echad Candelleth, south-west of the Crumbled Cellar, in Tâl Bruinen. You have discovered the diary of Sara Oakheart in the ruins of a burnt cottage in Tâl Bruinen and should show it to Candelleth at once.\n",
[1936]="700378DD\n1\tÉowyn has given you some writings from the search of Gríma's chambers, and wants you to find out where in the city these clues might refer.\t\n2\tTalk to Éowyn outside Meduseld\tÉowyn is outside Meduseld, in Edoras. You discovered several allies of Wormtongue working to hinder Éowyn's efforts in Edoras, and should report back to her that they will no longer be a problem.\n",
[1937]="7000B8E1\n1\tUse Leafy Bush\tDelossad is located south-east of Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen. Candelleth is sure that she has solved the riddle posed by the diary of Sara Oakheart, believing that the place of which she writes, Sithad, is an earlier form of the name Delossad, the ruins south-east of Echad Candelleth.\n2\tBring box of broken keys to Candelleth\tCandelleth is at her camp in Tâl Bruinen. You have recovered a box of broken keys from beneath a bush at the ruins of Delossad, known as Sithad in days now gone. You should bring the box to Candelleth.\n3\tBring box of broken keys to Merilos\tThe jeweller Merilos is at the Spire of Meeting in Rivendell. You have found a box full of broken keys buried sometime in the past at Delossad by Sara Oakheart and should bring them now to the jeweller Merilos, at Candelleth's insistence, to be remade.\n",
[1938]="7000D4BE\n1\tTalk to Elrond\030Collect Half of the Ring Narchuil\tElrond is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws. Gwathryn told you to take the half of Narchuil which you recovered to Elrond.\n2\tSpeak with Elrond to attend his Council\tElrond is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws. When you are ready to attend the Council of Narchuil, you should speak again with Elrond. This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.\n3\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws. You should speak at once with Elrond.\n",
[1939]="7003797E\n1\tTravel to the entrance of Brockbridge, in the Stonedeans\tThe town of Brockbridge is located to the south of Woodhurst. Herubrand has asked you to speak with his son Herefara in Brockbridge.\n2\tTalk to Herefara in Brockbridge\tHerefara is by the barricades on the southern side of Brockbridge. You have arrived at Brockbridge and should now speak with Herefara.\n3\tTalk to Thane Léoferth in the Mead Hall of Brockbridge\tThane Léoferth is in the Mead Hall of Brockbridge. Herefara has asked that you speak with the Thane before you investigate the turmoil in the Westfold.\n4\tTalk to Nona by Brockbridge\030Talk to Horn by Brockbridge\tHorn and Nona are on the southern side of the span, by Brockbridge, in the Stonedeans.\n5\tTalk to Corudan by Brockbridge\tCorudan is by the southern side of the span, in Brockbridge.\n6\tTravel to Helm's Dike, the entrance to the Deep, in the Westfold\tHelm's Deep is in the southern reaches of the Westfold. You and Corudan have decided to travel to Helm's Deep in search of the King, while Horn and Nona seek out the Falcon Clan raiding party.\n7\tTalk to Gamling at Helm's Dike\tGamling is at Helm's Dike, at the mouth of the Deep.\n",
[1940]="7000D4BD\n1\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at Tinnudir, off the eastern shore of Lake Nenuial, in Evendim. Elrond has asked you to return to Calenglad and begin a search for the Elf-lord Laerdan.\n",
[1941]="7003792B\n1\tTravel to the town of Entwade, in Kingstead, and help its people with their troubles\tThe town of Entwade is to the north-east of Edoras.\n2\tAfter you have helped the people of Entwade, travel to the entrance of Underharrow\tThe town of Underharrow is in Kingstead, to the south of Edoras. Éowyn has asked you to bring the news to Ellen Fremedon in Harrowdale that the people of Edoras will soon be sheltering on her lands.\n3\tTalk to Horn at the entrance to Underharrow\tHorn is at the entrance to Underharrow, in Harrowdale. Horn has come with you to Underharrow, and he wishes to speak with you by the entrance to that city.\n4\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon is in Underharrow, in Harrowdale.\n5\tPick up a barrel of swords from outside Ordwald's shop\tOrdwald, the blacksmith of Underharrow, has a shop to the south of the Mead Hall. Ellen Fremedon has asked you to carry a heavy barrel of swords from Ordwald's shop back to her.\n6\tPick up a barrel of armour from outside Ordwald's shop\tOrdwald, the blacksmith of Underharrow, has a shop to the south of the Mead Hall. Ellen Fremedon has asked you to carry a heavy barrel of armour from Ordwald's shop back to her.\n7\tPick up a barrel of spears from outside Ordwald's shop\tOrdwald, the blacksmith of Underharrow, has a shop to the south of the Mead Hall. Ellen Fremedon has asked you to carry a heavy barrel of spears from Ordwald's shop back to her.\n8\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon is outside the Mead Hall in Underharrow.\n",
[1942]="70037939\n1\tTalk to Horn at the entrance to Underharrow\tHorn is by the entrance to Underharrow. Ellen Fremedon has made her displeasure clear to you, and has nothing else to say.\n2\tCollect Orc sigils in Harrowdale (total: 6)\030Collect Warg teeth in Harrowdale (total: 6)\030Talk to Horn at the Dark Door, in Dunharrow\tOrcs and Wargs can be found throughout Harrowdale. Horn wants you to collect Orc sigils and Warg teeth from the invaders throughout Harrowdale.\n3\tBring the Orc sigils and the Warg teeth to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon is outside the Mead Hall of Underharrow, in Kingstead. You have collected Orc sigils and Warg teeth and should bring them to Ellen Fremedon to show her that she does not fight alone to defend her people.\n4\tTalk to Horn by the entrance to Underharrow\tHorn is at the entrance to Underharrow, in Kingstead. You have impressed Ellen Fremedon with your selfless actions on her behalf, and should let Horn know of the experience.\n",
[1943]="7000D4C4\n1\tSearch defeated Angmarim at Annúminas\tAngmarim can be found throughout Annúminas. Calenglad has suggested that you may find some information about Laerdan's whereabouts among the Angmarim.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\030Collect Amarthiel's Command\tCalenglad is at Tinnudir, north of Annúminas. You should return to Calenglad with Amarthiel's Command.\n",
[1944]="7000D4BF\n1\tSpeak to Forchon and enter Barad Tironn\tLaerdan may still be at Barad Tironn in Annúminas. Calenglad has instructed you to accompany Forchon to Barad Tironn to continue the search for Laerdan. Forchon can be found in Tinnudir, off the western shore of Lake Nenuial, in Evendim. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at Tinnudir, off the western shore of Lake Nenuial, in Evendim. You should speak with Calenglad and tell him of your deeds at Barad Tironn.\n",
[1945]="70037948\n1\tTravel to the entrance of Aldburg, in the Eastfold\tHorn will meet you at the entrance to Aldburg, in the Eastfold. You have agreed to journey to Aldburg to see how his home fares while Éomer rides with the King.\n2\tTalk to Horn at the entrance to Aldburg\tHorn is by the entrance to Aldburg, in the Eastfold. You have come to Aldburg with Horn, to see if Éomer's worries about his home are well-placed.\n3\tLook at the buildings in the south-west corner of Aldburg\030Talk to Páda in the south-west corner of Aldburg\030Look at the buildings by the Mead Hall in Aldburg\030Talk to Tirweld in Aldburg\tHorn wants you to explore the city of Aldburg so you can see if his first impression of its poor state was wrong.\n4\tTalk to Arcil inside the Mead Hall in Aldburg\tArcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg. You have learned that Aldburg has fallen into disrepair, and Arcil has had difficulty maintaining its rule in the absence of Éomer.\n5\tFind the camp of craftsmen Arcil sent to repair the Aldburg city walls\tThe craftsmen sent by Arcil to repair the walls of Aldburg have a camp outside the city, south-east of the walls. Arcil told you that if you think you can get the craftsmen to work, you are welcome to try.\n6\tTalk to a loutish worker\030Talk to a boorish worker\tThe craftsmen sent by Arcil are camping outside the walls of Aldburg, to the south-east. Arcil is unable to get the people to listen to him, so it comes to you to remind the craftsmen of their obligations.\n7\tTalk to Arcil in the Mead Hall of Aldburg\tArcil is inside the Mead Hall of Aldburg. You have gotten the workers outside Aldburg to begin working again, and should report of your success to Arcil.\n",
[1946]="7000D4CA\n1\tTalk to Gwathryn\tGwathryn is in Tármunn Súrsa, east of Carn Dûm, in Angmar. Calenglad has sent you to speak with Gwathryn, one of his scouts in Angmar.\n",
[1947]="7003794C\n1\tFind the waggon of craftsmen in the Everholt\tA number of craftsmen took a waggon from Aldburg into the Everholt to collect timber. Arcil has asked you to search the Everholt for the waggon of craftsmen, and to convince them to do the work they are supposed to do.\n2\tFollow the tracks south to the cave and complete 'Instance: The Missing'\tTracks lead south from the abandoned waggon in the Everholt to a cave entrance.\n3\tTalk to Nona in Aldburg\030Talk to Corudan in Aldburg\030Talk to Horn in Aldburg\tNona, Horn, and Corudan are in the town of Aldburg, in the Eastfold, and wish to speak with you.\n4\tTalk to Arcil in the Mead Hall of Aldburg\tArcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg, in the Eastfold. Horn has asked you to report of your success in the Everholt to Arcil in the Mead Hall.\n",
[1948]="70037956\n1\tTalk to Horn by the barrows outside Edoras, in Kingstead\tHorn will speak to you again by the barrows outside Edoras, as he did once before.\n2\tTalk to Horn by the barrows outside Edoras, and walk with him through the streets\tHorn is by the barrows outside Edoras, in Kingstead. Horn has asked you to tell him when you are ready to walk through the streets of Edoras with him and your companions.\n3\tTalk to Éowyn outside Meduseld, in Edoras\tÉowyn is outside Meduseld, in Edoras. You have learned that an ally of Wormtongue's attempted to sabotage the evacuation efforts, but may have fled the city.\n",
[1949]="7000D4C0\n1\tDefeat Tarkrîp poisoners (total: 4)\030Defeat Tarkrîp jailors (total: 2)\tSammath Baul is in Carn Dûm west from Tármunn Súrsa. Gwathryn has instructed you to thin the Tarkrîp horde and collect the key of Sammath Baul from Lozudurkh. The Shimmering Elf-stone will be able to be used in an upcoming objective of this quest to access the inspiration buff if you are playing solo or in a small fellowship.\n2\tCollect Sammath Baul Gate-key\030Use Gate-house Door\tLozudurkh resides in the Sammath Baul gate-house. The gate-house is left of the Sammath Baul gate and has two torches in front of it. You have yet to defeat Lozudurkh and obtain the key to Sammath Baul. Using the Elf-stone allows you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.\n3\tTalk to Gwathryn\030Collect Sammath Baul Gate-key\030Collect Shimmering Elf-stone\tGwathryn is at Tármunn Súrsa, east of Sammath Baul. You should return to Gwathryn with the gate-key to Sammath Baul.\n",
[1950]="7000D4C1\n1\tSpeak with Gwathryn and enter Sammath Baul\tGwathryn is at Tármunn Súrsa in Angmar. You should speak with Gwathryn when you are ready to enter Sammath Baul. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws. You should journey south and speak with Elrond.\n",
[1951]="7003795C\n1\tTravel to the entrance of Stoke, in the Broadacres\tThe town of Stoke is located north of Edoras, in the Broadacres. You have given Éowyn your word that you will travel to Stoke to find the ally of Wormtongue that fled the city. He wears a blood-red brooch, but otherwise his appearance remains unknown to you.\n2\tTalk to Corudan outside the entrance of Stoke, in the Broadacres\tCorudan has called a halt just outside the entrance to the town of Stoke. You should speak to Corudan and ask him what he has found.\n3\tBring the Blood-eye Brooch to Fríthild in the Mead Hall of Stoke\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You have pursued Wormtongue's secret ally to Stoke, but he escaped into the city and discarded the brooch by which you would know him. Now you must warn the Reeve of the danger he poses.\n4\tTalk to Wigbald by the southern entrance to Stoke\tWigbald is at the southern entrance to Stoke. Reeve Fríthild has heard your warning about the mysterious foe that may have come to Stoke, and thinks you should speak with Wigbald at the southern entrance to the city. He may have seen something.\n5\tWigbald thinks you should investigate the Norcrofts, in East Rohan, but your instincts tell you that Wormtongue's ally is still somewhere in Stoke.\t\n6\tWigbald thinks you should investigate the Norcrofts, in East Rohan, but your instincts tell you that Wormtongue's ally is still somewhere in Stoke.\t\n7\tTalk to Adgyth on the northern reaches of Stoke\tYou found a discarded helmet, and nearby a small child has sought to get your attention.\n8\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall of Stoke\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke, in the Broadacres. You have learned that a suspicious man left the town, heading west, and may have joined with the Orcs. You should report what the child Adgyth saw to the Reeve.\n",
[1952]="7003796E\n1\tThe camp called Bardh-dorám is to the west of Stoke. Reeve Fríthild has asked you to defeat Orcs and half-orcs at the camp of Bardh-dorám, and to keep alert for sign of their plans.\t\n2\tDefeat Orc and half-orc raiders from Bardh-dorám (7/8)\tThe camp called Bardh-dorám is to the west of Stoke. Reeve Fríthild has asked you to defeat Orcs and half-orcs at the camp of Bardh-dorám, and to keep alert for sign of their plans.\n3\tBring the torn map of Stoke to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall\tYou have found a torn map of Stoke, and should return it to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall.\n4\tTalk to Adgyth in the Mead Hall of Stoke\tAdgyth is in the Mead Hall of Stoke, with Reeve Fríthild. You have returned to Stoke to be greeted with troubling news: Adgyth stumbled upon a dead body.\n5\tExamine the body of slain Wigbald, in the eastern part of Stoke\tAdgyth says she found Wigbald's body on the eastern side of the town of Stoke.\n6\tReturn to the south gate of Stoke and look for the man who claimed to be Wigbald\tIf Wigbald's body lies in the tall grass on the eastern side of Stoke, who did you speak to at the south gate who claimed to be Wigbald?\n7\tTalk to Corudan outside the south gate of Stoke\tCorudan is outside the south gate of Stoke.\n8\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall of Stoke\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. Corudan has pieced together what must have happened to Wigbald, and you should relate this information to the Reeve.\n",
})
